<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran engages US in 'intensive' negotiations to avert fresh war outbreak</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a97cc3846ba259d15e109c3207643fc66223cf915c874e127154e16394581ffc</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T17:42:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-iran-engages-us-in-intensive-negotiations-to-avert-fresh-war-outbreak" /><summary type="html">Tehran on Monday said that the country was holding "intensive" indirect talks with Washington to avoid a fresh round of US attacks on Iran ahead of the US midterm elections this week. Foreign ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei shared Iranian plans to reopen blockaded energy corridor, the Strait of Hormuz, if the US were to meet its demands.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran offers deal on Hormuz Strait, Netanyahu wants to 'finish the job'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ca755c3fc7c4029f0e290a5da39548c3faed93e229d7d96b443977e080b2bb2</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T17:04:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-iran-offers-deal-on-hormuz-strait-netanyahu-wants-to-finish-the-job" /><summary type="html">Iran said Monday it had a two-day plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and resume nuclear talks with the United States, shortening a process originally expected to take seven days. Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he wanted to "finish the job" first. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Petition to ban French right-wing TV channel clears 500,000 signatures after racist killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59fca07746d89c764b0e466697f96b70b5aebce68cf46b198d1f2b5405b74458</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:53:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261102-petition-to-ban-french-right-wing-tv-channel-clears-500-000-signatures-after-racist-killing" /><summary type="html">A petition calling for right-wing television channel CNews to be taken off-air cleared half a million signatures on Monday after a Frenchman shot and killed a French national of Congolese origin and wounded seven others. The 39-year-old shooter is believed to have been an avid watcher of CNews, which is owned by ultra-conservative billionaire Vincent Bolloré and has been accused of promoting far-right anti-immigrant views.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>British adventurer arrives back at mother's home after 28-year journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44982cc0b0ce292ebf4a19e997148ea1a4fce7a62ac3f7ac9ba8083f95c4f57e</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:45:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-british-adventurer-arrives-back-at-mother-s-home-after-28-year-journey" /><summary type="html">British adventurer Karl Bushby enjoyed an emotional reunion with his mother and family on Monday, as he arrived back home after a 28-year, 50,000-kilometre trek from South America, crossing four continents on foot.</summary></entry><entry><title>What changes if Democrats win a majority in Congress?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bf075ae5ad86f73dd97e6b6e9eaf7a2e1eec5da8d88a98da53d52a9535e6f94</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:29:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-what-changes-if-democrats-win-a-majority-in-congress" /><summary type="html">Americans head to the polls on Tuesday for the US midterm elections, which could flip the majority in one or both houses of Congress from the Republicans to the Democrats. What would a Democratic majority mean for the country's political landscape, and how might Democrats move to keep President Donald Trump in check?</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>A musical overview of trans-European punk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:876628cc7cb8f1c2cc8b1d7282e73d778c7a643ce1e2b86eb5779d0d21cab26a</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:05:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261102-a-musical-overview-of-trans-european-punk" /><summary type="html">This week on arts24, we're bringing you a double dose of European punk. Elias Bender Rønnenfelt is a singer with Copenhagen's finest post-punk export, Iceage. The group is currently touring Europe, and he is stopping off in Paris this week to play the Pitchfork festival solo. We also welcome Chris Hughes from Fat Dog. Born in South London in 2020 during lockdown, Fat Dog have just released their second album "Cancel Me (I'm Tired)", which will thrill synth lovers and punk rockers alike. They are currently touring France and Europe.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's president begins process of coalition government negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdfef3bad2c79b4a052ba17f4812267a70d1e572484044eec7bee204164cd3a7</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-israel-s-president-begins-process-of-coalition-government-negotiations" /><summary type="html">Israel's President Isaac Herzog begins the process of coalition government negotiations this week. One possibility is for the centrist opposition bloc to form a government with the Arab parties, which would oust current Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Protests for and against such a coalition this weekend made it clear the Israeli public is divided over the idea.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scientists begin tests on human composting, an eco-friendly alternative to burials and cremation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d63fd07c1686b82191805dedfb2ec8ae64b657e181ef2d74ea5ae8abc1d3c70d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:41:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261102-scientists-begin-tests-on-human-composting-an-eco-friendly-alternative-to-burials-and-cremation" /><summary type="html">Humans have caused irreversible changes to our planet in their time on Earth, pollution that continues even in death. Cremation relies heavily on fossil fuels, while traditional burials take up land. So is there a more eco-friendly way to honour our loved ones? French scientists are exploring the possibility of composting human bodies, a process that returns those who have died to the earth. Our Down to Earth team reports.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Nine dead in small plane crash near Trump's Florida home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:969568aaea649db41dbef50c8aee59ae09537392bcc91978c649d9b8eb108d3a</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:33:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-nine-dead-in-small-plane-crash-near-trump-s-florida-home" /><summary type="html">Nine people were killed Sunday when the Learjet they were travelling in plummeted into a neighbourhood in southern Florida, just miles from US President Donald Trump's resort home of Mar-a-Lago, officials said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Inflation, war and corruption: Will anger at Trump see Republicans punished at midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9615ac5ee5e84b3f7ea086a566d347bd74a3edb7a0e4c8cb1936afb5e96fdbf</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:30:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-inflation-war-and-corruption-will-anger-at-trump-see-republicans-punished-at-midterms" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump and his Republican Party will make last-gasp pitches to US midterm voters Monday to hold back a predicted Democrat wave that could take over Congress and impose tight political constraints on the president for the first time in two years. With Trump's popularity at an historic low, many are predicting voters will punish the Republican Party at the polls. France 24's Philip Turle takes a closer look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Heading into the midterms, 'no US president in recent times has been as unpopular as Donald Trump'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19b75a656ce70ceb71606c7bb61e35d3e7facf1a05be3d76fdf3bf1d52b2cacd</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:25:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/heading-into-the-midterms-no-us-president-in-recent-times-has-been-as-unpopular-as-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics at Queen Mary University of London. He says that "Donald Trump is damaged goods at this point in his presidency." With this uncompromising assessment, Johnson takes us through the political forces shaping the 2026 US midterm elections. Far from assuming that Trump's formidable campaigning instincts can once again mobilize Republican voters, Johnson questions whether the president's political influence has become a liability for the very party he once transformed. He points to a potentially significant realignment within the American electorate. Economic grievances, rising living costs, trade disputes and disillusionment with the war in Iran appear, in Johnson's reading, to be weakening important elements of the coalition that sustained Trump's return to power. Particularly consequential is the possibility that Latino voters, agricultural communities and sections of the MAGA electorate may be reconsidering their political loyalties or withdrawing from electoral participation altogether.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia report fake emergency alerts after cyberattacks target apps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45e47bb3fdd1d8f0e82ab1ae17405177b5d62253fabd61d36fdd2171d0323d1d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:06:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-report-fake-emergency-alerts-after-cyberattacks-target-apps" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Ukraine and Russia said their emergency alert mobile apps had been targeted by cyberattacks, with users in Ukraine receiving false warnings of an imminent nuclear threat. Moscow said that hackers had sent fake emergency alerts after gaining access to the Russian Emergency Situations Ministry’s mobile app, and that efforts were ongoing to restore the app's functionality.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Will Gen Z enthusiasm help turn Michigan Senate blue?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:112cbd4e8450254c8815d0325d65c8c8234116ec0a2955296798e293936ed980</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:03:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-will-gen-z-enthusiasm-help-turn-michigan-senate-blue" /><summary type="html">Michigan’s Senate seat is a must-win for the Democratic Party as it seeks to take control of the upper house of Congress. There’s a surge of energy behind progressive candidate Abdul El-Sayed, especially among younger voters. But can Gen Z's enthusiasm translate into votes and help Democrats win a critical Senate seat?</summary></entry><entry><title>Could Argentina’s Patagonia become a haven for data centres?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6876fe33281b363caa8d4191ddf8edd77833897d40ec19418dcc6556de77042</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:16:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-could-argentina-s-patagonia-become-a-haven-for-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Around the world, citizens and lawmakers are increasingly pushing back against the construction of data centres, citing noise pollution, massive power consumption and general unsightliness. But Argentina's President Javier Milei wants more of them - and the government thinks it may have found an ideal location, in the vast open steppes of Patagonia.</summary></entry><entry><title>French school protests resume on smaller scale after autumn break</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe61e5eda7e8cf230d2901fd2b978fdef80cbd5fa09205fad7ba659e10ff940d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:15:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-french-school-protests-resume-on-smaller-scale-after-autumn-break" /><summary type="html">French high school student protests resumed on Monday on a ​much smaller scale than in past weeks as pupils returned from a two-week break, with youngsters trying to blockade a few high schools in Paris, Marseille and Rennes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sour grapes? Dems shocked as Haley Stevens breaks ranks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ba244cfb8f6d5350fb2b722276ee152b61936f31eda7a242f06457163fb241e</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:54:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-sour-grapes-dems-shocked-as-haley-stevens-breaks-ranks" /><summary type="html">France 24’s Fraser Jackson takes a look at the state of play one day ahead of crucial midterm elections in the US as both Democrats and Republicans make their final bids for votes. Meanwhile, Michigan Democrat Haley Stevens has rocked the state’s Senate race by endorsing Republican Mike Rogers over Democratic candidate Abdul El-Sayed. Stevens lost the Michigan Democrats' Senate primary to El-Sayed in a bitterly contested race, leading some to accuse her of sour grapes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Fresh wave of fridge cyberattacks hits European supermarkets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef6015c04ac55f46baf534da5fea6ddf11562bd8e72219b89649f594bbe9f380</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:40:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-fresh-wave-of-fridge-cyberattacks-hits-european-supermarkets" /><summary type="html">Stores and supermarkets across Belgium, Luxembourg, Finland, Estonia and Sweden all reported early Monday abrupt temperature spikes in their fridges and freezers in an apparent cyberattack targeting refrigeration units. The incidents follow a similar attack that hit hundreds of supermarkets across France in October, triggering food loss and fires.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italian journalists under police protection as threats rise across the country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba5193e3f5fb9bdc9c087e2e503c1396937ab366b037dc3fbce36e4e3966af7c</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:20:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-italian-journalists-under-police-protection-as-threats-rise-across-the-country" /><summary type="html">Italy is the European country with the largest number of journalists under police protection. There, journalism is a profession particularly susceptible to threats and intimidation, but the European Union's measures to protect press freedom are slow to be implemented. FRANCE 24's team has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: North Carolina farmers hit hard by inflation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d20dc230d46e147e26540b54a84b76ae901a8fb095b24143d932c1838b9c09e</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:13:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261102-us-midterm-elections-north-carolina-farmers-hit-hard-by-inflation" /><summary type="html">On the eve of the midterm elections, US President Donald Trump's unpopularity is impacting Republicans across the board. Many states with seats once considered Republican strongholds are now on shaky ground. One of them is North Carolina, a rural state where one in five jobs is tied to agriculture.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Michigan Democrat's endorsement of Republican ruffles critical Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba29646bd5476f89557a14ddb5dfadbe8e3e20692f2ed2d914eb7a846dafe46f</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:41:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-michigan-democrat-s-endorsement-of-republican-ruffles-critical-senate-race-1" /><summary type="html">A prominent Michigan Democrat endorsed Republican Mike Rogers on Sunday, giving President Donald Trump's Republicans an unexpected boost in a critical US Senate race two days before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress.</summary></entry><entry><title>'No political solution' to anger in France, expert says amid ongoing protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b41577d40f939948ecb27d5d4c01e1c0b8fc6ec1ef5083c41e60542264ef007</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:41:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261102-no-political-solution-to-the-anger-in-france-expert-says-amid-ongoing-protests" /><summary type="html">With the vast majority of French high schools reopening despite calls for new blockades, and the number of people attending weekend demonstrations down for the third week in a row, are the protests in France beginning to die out? We spoke to one political expert who says he believes they will, saying it is difficult to see who people are protesting against, given that the government has no majority in parliament.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>How Antonelli became Formula One's youngest world champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ce85f508b1dc073ec22241d20fe0fb989c918410dd8fc50352b1e1b4ffe103c</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:54:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-how-antonelli-became-formula-one-s-youngest-world-champion" /><summary type="html">A tearful Kimi Antonelli became Formula One's youngest world champion at 20 years and 68 ​days old on Sunday when he finished third for Mercedes in a red-flagged and restarted Mexico City Grand Prix won by Red Bull's Max Verstappen.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Michigan Democrat Haley Stevens defects from party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6e993507019585c10274d2c5ea5a0629569e5b8d3accae4cdc0faec41019b87</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:52:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-michigan-democrat-haley-stevens-defects-from-party" /><summary type="html">Democrats sought on Monday, November 2, to contain a rift in Michigan's US Senate race after one of their own crossed party lines to endorse the Republican candidate, as both parties made final pitches before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'More patients and fewer doctors': The struggle for maternity care in Afghanistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc37cdb446b110ea872e6078d395c95e93002868913aba77390573f5b99c5373</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:48:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-more-patients-and-fewer-doctors-the-struggle-for-maternity-care-in-afghanistan" /><summary type="html">Afghanistan has one of the highest maternal mortality rates in the world. Experts say on average, a woman dies every two hours from complications during childbirth. The problem has become more accute since the Taliban returned to power in 2021, with access to healthcare for Afghan women becoming increasingly difficult. FRANCE 24's team reports from on the ground.</summary></entry></feed>
